== Real headers ==

testdata/mainnet-653572.json   sha256 aba7a2ea57e1ebad9b614fc01306d8d99abd20e76797946c53bdfde08759dede
  Mainnet 653572..653649, 78 headers (Blossom activates at 653600), txids of 653572, 653577, 653581, 653600,
  653601, 653603. Pin: 653649 = 0000000002be3f100cba287ea383787dafeae18bdc4b7a5f32a38fe041f33b38 (main-checkpoints.txt)
testdata/mainnet-3436131.json  sha256 d62c5a0763e6e4f3b5dcf3dc28bfcb802cfc960df7938a4dc3522ee0f714fefc
  Mainnet 3436131..3436171, 41 headers (NU6.3), txids of 3436140, 3436159, 3436161, 3436162, 3436163, 3436166,
  3436170, 3436171 (coinbases v5 and v6). Pin: 3436171 = 000000000007ec04a25dc7552851b4cd512b71f9af26bfb77e4ff6b465c257fa,
  the last Mainnet checkpoint Zebra 6.3.0 ships
  Both fetched from https://api.blockchair.com/zcash/raw/block/<height>, one request per height, 2.2 s apart,
  09:24–09:31Z. Blockchair is not a primary source; the pins are. The builder refused any header whose SHA-256d
  differed from decoded_raw_block.hash, any break in hashPrevBlock, and a run not holding its pin.
testdata/testnet-299160.json   sha256 68afc3e42fbb8c50035963bf0caab826920e3f2d40e205953a4f4003533335cd
  Testnet 299160..299230, 71 headers (the minimum-difficulty rule starts at 299188; 299188, 299189 and 299202
  are at PoWLimit), txids of 299180, 299184, 299185, 299186, 299190, 299202. Pin: 299200 =
  00604b163e34bcbf447a5aed105cca5d8d4311afe435fdcec9b4f8bec5769c48 (test-checkpoints.txt)
  Read 09:42Z from the local zebrad 6.3.0 Testnet node (tools/regtest/zcash-testnet-up.sh) on its internal RPC,
  127.0.0.1:18242 inside WSL, with its cookie: getblockhash <h>, getblock <hash> 0 (raw block, header = first
  1487 bytes) and getblock <hash> 1 (txid list). The same builder checks applied.

Node calls made, all read-only: getblockhash and getblock (verbosity 0 and 1). getblockchaininfo was also called
four times at the start to see how far the sync had got; the fetcher then waited with getblockhash alone.

testdata/equihash-librustzcash.json sha256 c8bd578a5d470e77245e7257d5772652a57d2937ecdc1cf5edd2e0f8ffd0dd22

The converter and the header builder were throwaway programs outside the tree; the checks they made are the
ones listed above, and the tests re-check everything that matters from the recorded bytes (hashes, links, pins,
Equihash, nBits, Merkle roots).
